  "notes": [
    "Phone access uses More > Analysis hub > Chart context. There is no permanent closed-reader row. Tablet retains its toolbar entry; the reader moves below the whole chart at the single-column breakpoint.",
    "The core toolbar measurement includes Context. Native shells use their chart menu and keep the normal web toolbar absent. The original chart-fill, tray-overflow, phone-fold, expanded-strip and tablet-fit assertions are unchanged.",
    "The reader receives focus and reveals its header on explicit opening. Close restores a visible persistent opener, including after desktop-to-phone resize. Reader keys remain isolated from chart shortcuts.",
    "The exact ten-test Visual Intelligence suite still runs at all three viewports. Settings restoration now exercises the actual entry and numeric reader before and after reload. A mouse inspection scrolls the chart back into view after the inline reader reveal.",
    "The combined responsive report includes actual SPY Options held-build, selected strike 780, pin, scroll and same-instance checks in EN/ZH across all three viewports, plus the newly merged research-pane touch exit.",
    "The combined report deliberately skips duplicate multi-viewport transitions and viewport-inapplicable phone/desktop research cases; every supported viewport has its own placement and interaction evidence.",
    "All 24 PL6 crops and all five Options axis-label captures were regenerated from this integrated source. A previous dev-server attempt returned stale 404 routes; its failure images were retained outside the evidence packet, and a fresh owned dev cache produced the accepted captures.",
    "Terminal is dark-only. Browser data is from repository fixtures and intercepted test contracts; live production qualification is separate. Paper uses supplied screenshot metric values with illustrative chart artwork."
  ],
